---
title: "Block-level transclusion"
description: "Pulling one anchored section out of a shared file instead of the whole file."
---

`{{< include file.tmd >}}` splices a whole file in. Adding a `#fragment` narrows it
to **one anchored section** of that file:

```
{{< include _includes/shared-derivation.tmd#sec-bias-variance >}}
```

The section runs from the heading carrying the anchor to the next heading of equal
or shallower level, exactly as folding bounds it in the editor. Everything else in
the shared file stays where it is.

