{{< include _includes/shared-derivation.tmd#sec-bias-variance >}}

## A second section from the same file

Two fragments of one file are not a cycle, so a document can assemble several
sections from one shared source. This one carries a subsection, which comes along
because it sits *inside* the named section:

{{< include _includes/shared-derivation.tmd#sec-normal-equations >}}

## What it does not do

A fragment that names no section in the file is left literal and reported, rather
than silently expanding to the whole file or to nothing:

```
{{< include _includes/shared-derivation.tmd#sec-no-such-thing >}}
```

Click-to-source on any transcluded block opens the *shared* file at the line the
block really occupies there, not at the top of the file and not at the line it
happens to land on in this document.
